You are updating the ChartForge project.  
You must fix and enhance the Companies module and fully implement the AI agent “Dexter”.

Your tasks are divided into 3 major parts:

═════════════════════════════════════════════════
1) COMPLETE REWORK OF THE COMPANY MODULE (CRUD)
═════════════════════════════════════════════════

Current situation:
- Companies can be created but cannot be edited properly.
- Deletion does not work and is not desirable. We need INACTIVATION.
- The UCID system works, but the lifecycle must be improved.
- The current UI uses a side-panel for editing, which is insufficient.
- There is no protection against accidental inactivation.

► Replace DELETE with a complete SOFT-INACTIVATION workflow.

Required backend changes:

### BACKEND — FASTAPI + SQLAlchemy
Implement:
- POST /companies → create company
- GET /companies → list (filter active/inactive)
- GET /companies/{ucid}
- PUT /companies/{ucid} → update
- PATCH /companies/{ucid}/inactivate
- PATCH /companies/{ucid}/activate
- Add a required confirmation step:
  Endpoint must require:
      { "confirmation": "<company_name>" }
  If names do not match → fail (400).
- Soft delete fields:
    is_active: bool = True
    inactivated_at: datetime | null
    inactivated_by: user_id | null
- UCID rules:
  - UCID remains reserved for the same normalized name.
  - Reactivation reuses the same UCID.
  - If the legal name changes, generate a new UCID only if it is a *different company*, not a reactivation.

### FRONTEND — SvelteKit
Implement a complete UX overhaul:

1. Replace inline edit panel with:
   - A modal popup (“Edit Company”)
   - Tabs inside modal: Basic / Contact / Additional
   - Save/Cancel buttons
   - Validation using zod

2. Add “Inactivate Company” workflow:
   - Clicking the icon opens a modal:
        “To inactivate this company, type the company name:”
        - Input field
        - If match → enable Confirm
   - Show warnings:
        - If Master Chart exists
        - If mappings exist
        - If QuickBooks sync configured
        - If snapshots or imports depend on it

3. Add “Activate Company” workflow:
   - Same modal confirmation

4. Improve company list UI:
   - Active and Inactive tabs
   - Each company card shows:
       • UCID  
       • Industry  
       • Email  
       • Description  
       • Status badges (“Active”, “Inactive”)  
       • Actions: View | Edit | Inactivate/Activate

5. Add toast notifications for every action.

6. Add audit indicators:
   “Last updated by ___ on ___”
   “Inactivated on ___ by ___”

═════════════════════════════════════════════════
2) COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE “DEXTER” AI AGENT
═════════════════════════════════════════════════

Dexter currently exists only visually.  
You must implement the ENTIRE logic behind the agent:

-------------------------------------------------
A) PASSIVE MODE (LEARNING ENGINE)
-------------------------------------------------

Dexter must:
- Learn the company’s Master Chart
- Learn mappings, ledger imports, QuickBooks data
- Learn recurring patterns:
    vendor → account  
    contract → account  
    description patterns  
    amount patterns  
- Build embeddings using the configured Ollama model:
    qwen2.5-coder:1.5b-base  
  (loaded from .env variables)
- Maintain a per-company vector index
- Be triggered automatically on data import or user classification

Implement:

### Backend requirements:

Create service:
`app/ai/learning_engine.py`
with methods:
- ingest_master_chart(ucid)
- ingest_mappings(ucid)
- ingest_ledger(ucid)
- rebuild_embeddings(ucid)
- get_company_knowledge(ucid)

Store embeddings:
- Prefer pgvector, fallback to a local vector DB (Chroma or DuckDB).
- Maintain metadata: source, account, confidence, last_seen, company_ucid.

Add background tasks using:
- FastAPI BackgroundTasks OR Celery (if available)
- Rebuild embeddings on-demand or scheduled.

-------------------------------------------------
B) ACTIVE MODE (ASSISTANT)
-------------------------------------------------

Dexter must:
- Respond to chat
- Suggest accounts for new transactions
- Generate charts (JSON encoded + frontend rendering)
- Generate PDF or Excel reports
- Provide explanations for account selection
- Answer natural-language queries:
      “Show me expenses by category”
      “Which vendors map to account 6100?”
      “Summarize last month’s imports”

Endpoints required:
- POST /ai/chat
- POST /ai/suggest
- POST /ai/generate/chart
- POST /ai/generate/report
- GET  /ai/context/{ucid}

Dexter must use:
- Company embeddings
- Master Chart relationships
- Historical behavior patterns
- System heuristics

-------------------------------------------------
C) FRONTEND CHAT WIDGET
-------------------------------------------------

Complete the floating widget with:
- Open/close animation
- Message history (localStorage + server-side save optional)
- Quick action buttons:
    • “Explain this account”
    • “Suggest account”
    • “Generate chart”
    • “Generate report”
- Auto-scroll
- Feedback loading indicators
- Dark/light mode support

═════════════════════════════════════════════════
3) QUALITY IMPROVEMENTS, STABILITY, CONSISTENCY
═════════════════════════════════════════════════

Add the following:

### A) Event Logging (Audit Trail)
Create table:
audit_log:
    id
    timestamp
    user_id
    action
    entity_type (“company”, “mapping”, etc.)
    entity_id/ucid
    payload_json

Log events for:
- Company create
- Company update
- Company inactivate
- Company activate
- AI actions (suggestions, reports, chat requests)
- Sync operations

### B) Error visibility
- Show descriptive errors in toasts
- Backend must return structured errors:
    { "error": "Invalid confirmation", "expected": "MARAVILLA CLEANERS" }

### C) Caching
- Cache company list and AI context in frontend
- Revalidate on update

